  "context_pill": "Taxability of Agricultural and Sikkimese Income",
  "example_summary": "Analyzing the tax status of residential rent from farm land, nursery income, and Sikkimese individual earnings under the Income Tax Act.",
  "source_provision": "| Aspect / Receipt | Statutory Section | Legal Basis / Statutory Rule | Tax Treatment / Legal Consequence |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Farm Building Letting** | Section 2(1A) Explanation 2 | Rent derived from letting out a building on agricultural land for non-agricultural purposes (e.g. residential/business) | **Taxable** (Excluded from Agricultural Income) |\n| **Nursery Seedling Sales** | Section 2(1A) Explanation 3 | Income derived from saplings or seedlings grown in a nursery | **Exempt u/s 10(1)** (Deemed Agricultural Income regardless of basic land operations) |\n| **Sikkimese Individual Income** | Section 10(26AAA) | Income accruing/arising from within the State or dividend/interest on securities | **Exempt u/s 10(26AAA)** (Fully exempt from tax) |\n\n> [!IMPORTANT] Scope of Section 2(1A) Explanation 2\n> Any building income derived from use for any purpose other than agriculture (such as residential accommodation for workers or commercial use) fails the agricultural test and is treated as standard taxable income.\n\n> [!NOTE] Scope of Section 2(1A) Explanation 3\n> Carrying out basic operations on land (ploughing, tilling, sowing) is NOT a prerequisite for nursery seedling income to qualify as exempt Agricultural Income.\n\n> [!WARNING] Scope of Section 10(26AAA)\n> Exemption for a Sikkimese individual covers income arising from within the State and global dividend/interest on securities, provided the individual qualifies as a Sikkimese resident under statutory criteria.",
